/* Approved privacy text and the launch Cookie Policy. No tracking or consent code. */
pages.privacy=()=>pageHead('Privacy and data protection','AyudaGrow Privacy Policy','How we handle personal information across our website, enquiries and customer accounts.')+section(`<article class="editorial policy-copy"><p>Website: <a href="https://www.ayudagrow.com">https://www.ayudagrow.com</a>  |  Last updated: 13 November 2026</p><p>Ayuda Grow LLC operates AyudaGrow. This policy explains how we collect and use personal information when you visit our website, enquire about our services, sign up or manage your account.</p><h2>Who we are and how to contact us</h2><p>Ayuda Grow LLC is registered in Florida. Business address: 7901 Fourth Street North, St. Petersburg, Florida, United States. We are responsible for the personal information used to manage our website enquiries and customer relationships. For privacy questions or requests, email <a href="mailto:admin@ayudagrow.com">admin@ayudagrow.com</a> or call <a href="tel:+18764800413">+1 876-480-0413</a>.</p><h2>Who this policy covers</h2><p>This policy covers website visitors, prospective customers and account holders. Businesses using AyudaGrow are responsible for explaining how they use information about their own customers. Requests concerning those records should be directed to the relevant business.</p><h2>Information we collect</h2><p>Signup forms collect your first name, last name, phone number, account email and business name. Enquiries and account administration can also include correspondence, chat messages, service requirements, support information and subscription or payment records. Visiting the website or using embedded forms and chat can generate technical information, such as your IP address, browser, device and connection details.</p><p>Please provide only information needed for your enquiry or service. Do not submit passwords, payment-card details, patient information or other sensitive customer records through website chat, general enquiries or signup forms. Without the contact or account details needed for a request, we may be unable to respond or provide the requested service.</p><h2>How we use information</h2><p>We use personal information to respond to enquiries, follow up on services you request, manage signup and onboarding, administer accounts and billing, provide support and send service communications. We also use relevant records to meet legal obligations and address payment or service disputes.</p><p>Our handling of information depends on the purpose and applicable law, including steps requested before entering a contract, providing contracted services, meeting legal obligations and obtaining consent where required. Permission to receive promotions is separate from signup and service communications. You can contact <a href="mailto:admin@ayudagrow.com">admin@ayudagrow.com</a> to withdraw marketing permission or ask us to stop promotional contact.</p><h2>Payments</h2><p>Payments are completed through Stripe. Payment-card details are entered on Stripe, not in the AyudaGrow signup form. We use relevant payment confirmations and subscription information to administer your account. Stripe explains its handling of personal information at <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy">https://stripe.com/privacy</a>.</p><h2>Website chat and AI</h2><p>Our website assistant uses artificial intelligence to answer general questions about AyudaGrow. Messages and contact details you choose to provide are processed through HighLevel and the AI service providers supporting the assistant to generate responses and handle your enquiry. Authorised team members may review conversations to respond, provide support or follow up on your request.</p><p>AI responses can contain mistakes. For help from a person or confirmation of service details, email <a href="mailto:admin@ayudagrow.com">admin@ayudagrow.com</a> or call <a href="tel:+18764800413">+1 876-480-0413</a>. Chat transcripts are kept for 12 months after the conversation ends, subject to the limited exceptions below.</p><h2>Who receives information</h2><p>We use Hostinger for website hosting, HighLevel for CRM, embedded signup and chat services, and Stripe for payments. The AI providers supporting HighLevel process chat information as needed to operate the assistant. Business email services carry correspondence you send to us. Relevant information may also be disclosed where legally required or necessary to establish, exercise or defend legal claims.</p><p>We do not sell personal information. We do not share phone numbers or marketing consent with third parties for their own marketing or promotional purposes. Service providers may process contact information on our behalf to deliver the services described in this policy.</p><h2>International processing</h2><p>Personal information may be processed outside your country. HighLevel lists infrastructure in the United States and support processing in India. Its Data Processing Agreement sets out confidentiality, security, subprocessor and transfer provisions, including jurisdiction-specific safeguards where applicable. The services used determine which subprocessors handle information.</p><p>HighLevel’s processing terms and current subprocessor list are available at <a href="https://www.gohighlevel.com/data-processing-agreement">https://www.gohighlevel.com/data-processing-agreement</a> and <a href="https://www.gohighlevel.com/sub-processors">https://www.gohighlevel.com/sub-processors</a>. Contact <a href="mailto:admin@ayudagrow.com">admin@ayudagrow.com</a> for questions about the handling of your information across borders.</p><h2>Cookies and browser storage</h2><p>The website uses session storage to remember page position and selections. Embedded signup forms, the chat widget and Stripe checkout may also use cookies, browser storage and connection information to operate their services. Your browser settings allow you to manage cookies and clear stored data. Blocking storage can affect form, chat or checkout functionality.</p><p>We do not deploy Google Analytics 4 or Meta advertising tags on this website. This statement concerns our website tags and does not mean embedded services operate without cookies or technical data collection. We will update this policy before introducing new analytics or advertising tools and provide consent controls where required.</p><h2>Security</h2><p>We use reasonable technical and organisational safeguards to protect personal information against unauthorised access, misuse, loss or disclosure. No internet service or storage system can guarantee complete security. Keep your login details private and contact us if you suspect unauthorised use of your account.</p><h2>Children</h2><p>AyudaGrow is a business service and is not directed at children. If you believe a child has provided personal information through our website, contact <a href="mailto:admin@ayudagrow.com">admin@ayudagrow.com</a> so we can review and address it.</p><h2>How long we keep information</h2><p>Our retention periods are based on the type of record and the purpose for keeping it:</p><table><caption>Personal information retention periods</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Information</th><th scope="col">Retention period</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Website chat transcripts</th><td>12 months after the conversation ends.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Enquiries and leads that do not become customers</th><td>24 months after the last meaningful contact. Automated messages sent by us do not restart this period.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Active account information</th><td>For the customer relationship, while needed to provide and administer the service.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Closed account operational data</th><td>90 days after closure, then deleted from active systems.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Marketing opt-out records</th><td>Indefinitely, limited to what is needed to prevent further marketing, such as the email address or phone number, channel and opt-out date.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Necessary billing and tax records may be retained separately for applicable legal and accounting requirements. Records needed for an actual dispute or legal obligation may be kept for that purpose. These exceptions do not require retaining an entire customer profile.</p><p>Archived provider backups are separate from active systems. HighLevel’s processing terms provide for retained customer data to remain protected and isolated from further processing, except as legally required. A valid deletion request may require action before a normal retention period ends.</p><h2>Your privacy requests and complaints</h2><p>Depending on applicable law, you may request access to or correction of your information, deletion, restriction of or objection to processing, or withdrawal of consent. Email <a href="mailto:admin@ayudagrow.com">admin@ayudagrow.com</a> with the request and the account or interaction it concerns. We may ask for information needed to verify your identity. Please do not send passwords or payment-card details.</p><p>We handle requests within the periods required by applicable law. Some information may need to be retained for legal reasons. You can also complain to the relevant data protection authority, including Jamaica’s Office of the Information Commissioner where Jamaican law applies: <a href="https://www.oic.gov.jm">https://www.oic.gov.jm</a>.</p><h2>Changes to this policy</h2><p>We publish updates on this page and revise the last-updated date. Where legally required, we also notify affected account holders of material changes.</p><p>For more about cookies and browser storage, read our <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>.</p></article>`);
pages.cookies=()=>pageHead('Cookies and browser storage','Cookie Policy','How browser storage supports website navigation, signup, chat and checkout.')+section(`<article class="editorial policy-copy">
<p>Last updated: 13 November 2026</p>
<p>This Cookie Policy explains cookies and similar browser storage used in connection with www.ayudagrow.com, operated by Ayuda Grow LLC. Read it alongside our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>, which explains personal information, retention and your rights.</p>
<h2>What cookies and browser storage do</h2>
<p>Cookies are small files stored by your browser. They can help a service recognise a browser, maintain a session or remember preferences. Session storage and local storage also hold information in your browser. Session storage normally lasts for a tab session, while local storage can remain after you close the browser. Browser session-restoration settings can affect how long session information remains available.</p>
<p>Some storage is set by the website you visit. Other storage is set by providers whose forms, chat or payment services you use. A provider's general cookie policy can describe services beyond those used on AyudaGrow.</p>
<h2>Website navigation storage</h2>
<p>AyudaGrow uses the session-storage entry <code>ayudaVisits:clean-v1</code> to remember page routes, scroll position and selected interface controls. This helps the Back and Forward buttons return you to your previous place. It holds up to 100 saved visit entries in the browser session. Clearing site data removes the saved navigation state.</p>
<h2>Signup forms and AI chat</h2>
<p>Our signup forms and AI chat are provided through HighLevel. These embedded services may use cookies, local or session storage and technical connection information to maintain their sessions and operate the forms and conversations. Information you submit is handled as described in our Privacy Policy.</p>
<p>Storage set by embedded providers has its own lifetimes and controls. Our 12-month chat-transcript retention period concerns conversation records; it is not a claim that every chat cookie lasts 12 months. HighLevel describes its wider use of these technologies in its <a href="https://www.gohighlevel.com/cookies-policy">Cookie Policy</a>.</p>
<h2>Stripe checkout</h2>
<p>When you continue to Stripe checkout, Stripe uses cookies and similar technologies for payment functionality, security and fraud prevention. Its services can also use functional or other storage depending on the service and choices available. See <a href="https://stripe.com/legal/cookies-policy">Stripe's Cookie Policy</a> for purposes, durations and available controls.</p>
<h2>Analytics and advertising</h2>
<p>We do not deploy Google Analytics 4 or Meta advertising tags on this website. This does not mean our embedded providers operate without cookies or technical data collection. If we introduce analytics or advertising tools, we will update this policy and provide consent controls where required.</p>
<h2>Your choices</h2>
<p>You can use your browser's privacy settings to inspect, block or delete cookies and clear site data, including local and session storage. Settings may need to be changed separately for each browser, device and provider domain. Use any privacy controls offered by the provider when using its service.</p>
<p>Blocking or deleting storage can reset saved page positions and selections, interrupt chat sessions or affect signup and checkout. Browser settings do not delete records already submitted to AyudaGrow or its service providers. To request access to or deletion of personal information, contact us using the details below.</p>
<h2>Changes and contact</h2>
<p>We update this page when our use of these technologies changes and revise the last-updated date.</p>
<p>Ayuda Grow LLC<br>7901 Fourth Street North, St. Petersburg, Florida, United States<br>Email: <a href="mailto:admin@ayudagrow.com">admin@ayudagrow.com</a><br>Phone: <a href="tel:+18764800413">+1 876-480-0413</a></p>
</article>`);
render();
